STATE

  Version 0.3.1 on dev (W13). Phase P2b (disposable KVM/QEMU `tam-pane`
  DRM/KMS verification) is complete with zero live host changes
  (`upstream/2026-11-27-phase-p2b-tam-pane-vm-verification.md`):
  - Verified `tam-pane` `0.2.14` on DRM/KMS (`tty4`), `sd-login` automatic
    `seat0` session discovery (zero manual `register-session`), `tty7`
    interactive console prompt lockout/unlock/picker, `tam-hide` zero-flag
    auto-discovery, cross-VT handoff + `wl_seat` VT-resume behavior, live
    `SIGHUP` `passcodes.db` reload + corrupt-DB preservation, compositor exit
    T4b fail-closed return to `tty7`, and `SIGKILL` resilience on both
    `tam-hide` and `tam-hided`.
  - Fixed two real-world defects caught in the VM:
    - Default `lock_vt` moved from `6` to `7` (`src/tam-hided.c`,
      `systemd/tam-hided.service`) to stay outside `systemd-logind`'s
      `NAutoVTs=6` / `ReserveVT=6` range so `agetty` never races onto the lock
      VT.
    - Handled `POLLHUP | POLLERR | POLLNVAL` on `prompt.fd` and `watcher` fd in
      `src/tam-hided.c`, eliminating a 100% CPU busy loop on TTY hangup.
  - Verified host regression suites (`make clean && make all test test-headless`
    and `make clean && make USE_SYSTEMD=0 all test`) pass cleanly with `-Werror`.

